// @@@ If the index is within valid range (0 to size of the list), and the role is not null, then for every position from the index to the old size of the list, the element at the next position is either null and the old element at this position was null, or the element at the next position is equal to the old element at this position.
--------------------
// @@@ If the index is non-negative, less than or equal to the size of the list, and the role is not null, then for every valid index from the insertion point to the old size of the list, the element at the next position is either null and the old element at this index was null, or it is equal to the old element at this index.
